{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs9zcXm7p5S3fyfy8RqY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Sitting 007 is recorded, but the lane needs one more short text round. Two text defects, one in LLR-300 and one in SR-237, keep most of the approvals from landing in this sitting.\n\nThere are three commits: the verdict (`f64fb146`), the re-attestation (`2a6c1d91`) and the approval act (`88b51727`). All carry `WI: WI-834` and passed the commit hooks.\n\n**What I checked:** the lane changed only tests and spine rows, no shipped code.\n- The four affected suites gave `222 passed, 4 skipped`.\n- The skips are a POSIX-only test and three consent tests that need a pseudo-terminal, which Windows lacks. I read those tests but could not run them.\n- Every return from sitting 006 is answered:\n  - the lease-release test now exists;\n  - all three loop routes are driven through a refusal;\n  - LLR-047, SR-046 and the new LLR-320..322 and TC-343..345 rows describe the part C/D behaviour;\n  - TC-342 links to its LLR.\n\n**The two new defects:**\n- **LLR-300's close-down timing:** the row says the instruction comes at the first event of a window and every twentieth after, with SessionStart counted as one of those events. The code tells it at *every* SessionStart and counts only the other monitored events, per session. A build that follows the row text would fail TC-339's own test.\n- **SR-237's rewording:** \"not retaining a session whose prior use predates that window's end\" is no longer tied to resuming after the window. Read literally, it now forbids the in-window wrap-up resume that SR-227 allows, which brings back the contradiction round 001 fixed. The previously approved wording was fine.\n\n**amendment: `VERDICT: MEANING rows=8`.** I would bless six rows; LLR-300 and SR-237 are not blessed. I tried the SR and LLR copies first, and each was refused, naming only the row I left unblessed.\n- **Re-attested:** TC-316 and TC-321.\n- **Blessed but not anchored:** SR-046 (held by SR-237), and LLR-047, LLR-270 and LLR-301 (held by LLR-300).\n- **One draft:** fix both sentences. This is text only; the code and tests already behave correctly.\n\n**first-approval: `OUTCOME: RETURN rows=17`.** 16 rows approve; TC-339 returns, because it verifies LLR-300's unblessed text and repeats the same timing error.\n- **Flipped:** TC-341 and TC-342 only.\n- **Approved but not flipped:** LLR-316..322, because flipping them needs the LLR registry copy that LLR-300 holds. TC-335..338 and TC-343..345 then wait on those parents.\n\nThe next sitting should clear everything once those three short corrections land.\n\nOne observation, not a return: no row states the content of dev-setup's `claude setup-token` consent text. It falls under LLR-320's general \"offers each missing setup item\", and a test declines it and checks nothing changed.\n\nThe `.requested` marker is left untracked for the coordinator."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":877,"cache_read_input_tokens":350895,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":877},"output_tokens":747,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8d8d1fbc-6a42-4a02-9ec0-8f8d2b61c24c","uuid":"9c7cfa20-64b5-4415-bb33-1644dd4ff2b3","timestamp":"2026-10-09T18:43:13.271Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs9zcEtyiKLY8QG2gULP"}
